   "widgets_values": [
    "HaDeS MOSS Suite - Compare Models (the seventh video tutorial)\n\n1. MOSS Compare Sampler: SFT, Base, the sixth video's TEST recipe and Bulle d'Encre with the same prompt,\n   latent, seed and settings, on one sheet. Labels come from what each model carries (its file, a merge, its\n   LoRAs), the footer from what they share. Each column is the MOSS KSampler's image of that model; it is not\n   faster than four KSamplers and needs no more memory (RESULTS: 66-68 s for the four, ~31.7 GB VRAM).\n   A MOSS Turbo LoRA on the turbo input applies to every column.\n\n2. (muted) A LoRA at four strengths: Bulle d'Encre's LoRA (extract it first: LoRA Toolkit example, rank 64,\n   export_filename bulle_extracted) on its base, off / 0.5 / 0.8 / 1.0, 15 steps, euler. Against Bulle d'Encre\n   itself (1 = another seed): off 0.86, 0.5 0.74, 0.8 0.59, 1.0 0.26: strength is not linear.\n   blind: panels shuffled and numbered; the key is in info and in the PNG, never on the sheet;\n   blind_seed gives a new order of the same images.\n\n3. (muted) MOSS Compare Sheet: any images side by side, here two seeds of Base, labelled from each\n   KSampler's info. To use a muted group: select it, Ctrl+M."
   ],
   "properties": {}
